0001: # irl/URL Agency — Product Requirements Document
0002: 
0003: ## 1. Product Overview
0004: 
0005: irl/URL is a creative agency portfolio for a studio working in design, brand, fashion, art and product. The site presents positioning, selected work, services, philosophy, team and contact through a single continuous scroll experience backed by an immersive background field.
0006: 
0007: The central experience on the home route is a fixed full-screen visual field at the back, with nine content chapters that fade and slide in as the visitor scrolls. There are no separate page loads; scrolling drives visual changes and content swaps, with a left-aligned chapter label that animates in and an indicator that shows progress through the chapters. Work and team items open full-screen editorial overlays containing rich imagery, video and long-form text.
0008: 
0009: The product feels cinematic, minimal and tactile: dark canvas, white ink, accent orange `#F37330`, bold sans with serif and pixel details, large display typography, slow eased transitions, and interaction that rewards hover and scroll.
0010: 
0011: ## 2. Audience and Core Experience
0012: 
0013: - **Primary audience:**
0014:   - Brands, creators and partners seeking product creation, brand elevation and phygital production.
0015:   - Fans and press exploring case studies across fashion, gaming, music and sport.
0016:   - Prospective team and collaborators reviewing philosophy and credibility.
0017: 
0018: - **Main user goals:**
0019:   - Quickly understand what irl/URL does and its taste-level through intro copy and tagline.
0020:   - Browse work by name, see short descriptor on hover, open a case study and consume its story with images and video.
0021:   - Review services, about, mission, purpose, vision statements.
0022:   - Meet team members and see individual bios, titles, selected client logos and portrait video.
0023:   - Contact via email and follow social links.
0024: 
0025: - **Core user flows:**
0026:   - Land on `/` → see loading indicator → welcome chapter appears → scroll down → indicator progresses → work list appears → hover work item reveals descriptor → click opens case overlay → scroll case content → close returns to work.
0027:   - From any section → open menu via top-right trigger → choose `Work`, `Services`, `About`, `Team` → view jumps to that chapter → menu closes.
0028:   - Scroll through services grid → about narrative → mission → purpose → vision → team list → contact outro.
0029:   - From team list → hover profile item → click opens profile overlay with video, bio and logos → close returns to team.
0030:   - From outro → click `contact@irl-url.com` → mail client → click social links → new tab to external profiles.
0031: 
0032: - **Important emotional and usability qualities:**
0033:   - Continuous and fluid — no hard cuts between chapters, only camera and content morphs.
0034:   - Editorial restraint — sparse copy, large negative space, left-gutter labels, uppercase descriptors.
0035:   - Tactile and product-focused — imagery hero-sized, videos with controls, scope lists explicit.
0036:   - Fast orientation — menu and indicator always give location, logo always returns to top.
0037: 
0038: ## 3. Global Design System
0039: 
0040: - **Typography:**
0041:   - Display sans for primary headings:
0042:     - Weight `400` for work and team list items.
0043:     - Size `80px` for work/team links on desktop, smaller on narrow viewports.
0044:     - Line height `1` for large links, `1.2em` for service descriptions, `100%` for descriptor hover text.
0045:     - Tracking tight for display.
0046:   - Number markers:
0047:     - Pixel-style font for service numbers.
0048:     - Size `34px`.
0049:   - Label font:
0050:     - Serif for small labels in services.
0051:   - Body:
0052:     - Base `16px` over `1` line height, antialiased, with normalization for headings, paragraphs and lists.
0053:   - Font assets available locally:
0054:     - `/assets/fonts/pixel.otf`
0055:     - `/assets/fonts/sans.ttf`
0056:     - `/assets/fonts/serif.ttf`
0057:   - Heading side labels use bold for first syllable, e.g. `Wel` in `Welcome`, and sit left with top offset.
0058:   - Main chapter headlines have max widths between `520px` and `880px` for readability.
0059: 
0060: - **Color tokens:**
0061:   - Canvas: near-black dark for background field behind content.
0062:   - Ink primary: white `#ffffff` for headings, menu, body copy and close icons.
0063:   - Ink muted: white at reduced opacity for secondary descriptions.
0064:   - Accent: orange `#F37330` for theme color, tile color, progress and focus.
0065:   - Overlay surface: dark high-opacity black covering viewport for menu, case and profile overlays.
0066: 
0067: - **Spacing, layout, gutters, radii, borders, shadows, elevation:**
0068:   - Desktop content padding typical `8% 4.6% 8% calc(9.2% + 72px)` for narrative chapters, `8% calc(9.2% + 72px)` for list chapters.
0069:   - Left gutter for side label near `9.2% + 72px` at `8%` from top, fixed when chapter active.
0070:   - Section height `100vh` fixed for each chapter on desktop while scroll track drives progression.
0071:   - Scroll track height `1400vh` invisible driving chapter progression.
0072:   - List item spacing `60px` bottom margin, centered vertically with top padding.
0073:   - Services grid uses three columns on desktop, each roughly one third width and one third height, with side padding `0 60px 0 50px`, last item wide at two thirds and max `480px`.
0074:   - Radii minimal, squared imagery.
0075:   - Borders subtle `1px` for overlay edges where applied.
0076:   - Shadows soft glow for preloader logo.
0077: 
0078: - **Shared visual component styles:**
0079:   - Chapter label:
0080:     - Fixed near top left, initially transparent and offset with `translateY(20px)` and slight skew, then opaque and settled when chapter active.
0081:     - Transition `0.6s` with ease `cubic-bezier(0.215,0.61,0.355,1)` and short delay.
0082:     - Uppercase with first syllable bold.
0083:   - Work and team links:
0084:     - Large display size.
0085:     - Descriptor appears below link on hover as uppercase `24px` line `100%`, initially hidden with opacity and vertical offset, revealed on hover with eased transition.
0086:   - Service item:
0087:     - Number absolute left top `34px`.
0088:     - Description `24px` line `1.2em`.
0089:     - Final tailored note `18px` max `480px`.
0090:   - Close button:
0091:     - X formed by two thin `40x4` line graphics.
0092:     - Includes hidden text `close` for assistive tech.
0093:   - Progress circle for preloader uses stroke dash array driven by percentage.
0094: 
0095: - **Shared product/UI component patterns:**
0096:   - Intro hero: side label plus large headline near middle with bottom copy two columns.
0097:   - List hero: centered list of large typographic links with hover descriptor.
0098:   - Services grid: three-column wrap becoming fewer columns on narrow.
0099:   - Narrative chapter: headline plus large paragraph plus copy columns.
0100:   - Case overlay: cover figure full width with title and subtitle, intro split two columns (about copy plus scope list), then mixed rows of single, double and triple media.
0101:   - Profile overlay: split layout with left text stack and right video figure.
0102:   - Progress indicator: dots plus hover label showing section name.
0103: 
0104: - **Motion language:**
0105:   - Generic transitions `0.3s` for links and buttons.
0106:   - Chapter label entrance `0.6s` cubic-bezier `(0.215,0.61,0.355,1)`.
0107:   - Menu open fades main content to invisible.
0108:   - Indicator label appears with `66ms` delay on enter, hides with `400ms` fade.
0109:   - Case and profile overlays close with `450ms` animation before disappearing.
0110:   - Narrative content appears with a pause after section change before fully visible, camera updates quickly after scroll.
0111:   - Preloader logo morph animation `1s` with paths morphing and translating, looping `4s` indefinite during loading.
0112:   - Outline focus visible appears with `2px` solid offset `4px`.
0113: 
0114: - **Global responsive system:**
0115:   - Desktop threshold around `1101px` uses fixed full-viewport chapter system.
0116:   - Below threshold uses natural flow with auto heights, similar content but stacked.
0117:   - Edge padding percentage-based.
0118:   - Touch targets at least `40px` for menu trigger.
0119:   - No horizontal overflow at `320px` on any route.
0120:   - Full-width media scales to container with aspect preserved.
0121: 
0122: - **Image/media treatment:**
0123:   - Cover images full width of overlay, alt descriptive `"{Title} cover"`.
0124:   - Case images alt `Project visual`.
0125:   - Team images portrait `980x1080`, video `1080x1168`, duration about `12` to `16` seconds, codec `h264`.
0126:   - Work assets mixed `jpg`, `png`, `webp` local under `/assets/pages/` and `/assets/images/work/`.
0127:   - Videos local `mp4` with controls in case, autoplay muted loop for team profiles, muted hover preview in background for work and team lists.
0128:   - Critical assets warmed from cache including map texture and cube models.
0129:   - Lightbox placeholder low quality not required, but eager load for hero and lazy potential for grid.
0130: 
0131: ## 4. Global Accessibility Requirements
0132: 
0133: - **Keyboard reachability:**
0134:   - All interactive controls reachable: logo link, menu trigger, navigation links, work links, team links, case and profile close buttons, indicator dots, social links, email links, videos with controls.
0135: 
0136: - **Visible focus:**
0137:   - All controls show focus ring `2px solid currentColor` offset `4px` when focused via keyboard.
0138: 
0139: - **Heading structure:**
0140:   - Case and profile overlays each have one top heading for title.
0141:   - Chapters use side `h3` labels plus large `h2` headlines, order preserved without skipping inside surface.
0142: 
0143: - **Landmarks:**
0144:   - Persistent header at top.
0145:   - Main landmark for chapters.
0146:   - Navigation landmark for overlay menu.
0147:   - Figure landmark for media with captions where applicable.
0148:   - Menu list for navigation links.
0149: 
0150: - **Accessible names:**
0151:   - Logo link has hidden text `irl/URL`.
0152:   - Menu trigger has hidden text `menu`, controls site navigation and expands or collapses.
0153:   - Navigation overlay hidden when closed and visible when open, communicated via `aria-hidden`.
0154:   - Case close button label `Close case study`, profile close `Close team profile`.
0155:   - Indicator dots labeled by section name, inner progress indicator hidden from assistive tech.
0156:   - Social links labeled `Instagram`, `Twitter`, `LinkedIn` and contact link labeled `contact@irl-url.com`.
0157:   - Cover images alt `"{Title} cover"`, case images alt `Project visual`, team logos alt `"{Name} client logos"`, team portrait provides poster fallback.
0158:   - Preloader hidden label via visually hidden spans.
0159: 
0160: - **Alt text:**
0161:   - Meaningful imagery has descriptive alt, decorative icons and separators hidden when appropriate, SVG logos decorative but still have hidden text fallback.
0162: 
0163: - **Contrast:**
0164:   - White text on dark canvas retains strong contrast for large display and mono labels, service numbers also high contrast.
0165: 
0166: - **Reduced motion:**
0167:   - When visitor prefers reduced motion, fixed transforms and infinite looping animations reduce, scroll becomes instant, content appears without skew or prolonged stagger.
0168: 
0169: - **State:**
0170:   - Menu open makes main content invisible and inert.
0171:   - Case and profile overlays reset scroll to top when opened, show loading placeholder until images ready, then show ready content.
0172:   - Indicator active dot reflects current chapter, previous dots marked as passed, upcoming as pending.
0173:   - Preloader removed from view after loading completes.
0174: 
