le":"Every top-level section belongs to the expected scaffold; headings such as Assets and Visuals are subsections within Acceptance Criteria rather than non-standard top-level sections."}},"summary":{"overall_rationale":"The PRD is coherent, well-formatted, standalone, and follows the expected scaffold without replica framing or warning-level organization issues. It fails only R4 because several requirements document concrete implementation internals, including loading choices, manifest files, DOM identifiers and wrappers, DOM removal, and HTML rendering structure."}}
